From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:56:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] luks2 tests: the EFI loader is in /boot/system now

Since "Move bootloaders around somewhat." (d1231c1ac9), the haiku
package puts the EFI loader at /boot/system/haiku_loader.efi, where
Installer's "Install EFI loader" takes it from, instead of in
data/platform_loaders. guest-ui-test.sh compares the loader on the ESP
with that file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/tests/system/luks2/qemu/guest-ui-test.sh | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/tests/system/luks2/qemu/guest-ui-test.sh b/src/tests/system/luks2/qemu/guest-ui-test.sh
index 58eae9ceb4..9803968ebb 100755
--- a/src/tests/system/luks2/qemu/guest-ui-test.sh
+++ b/src/tests/system/luks2/qemu/guest-ui-test.sh
@@ -201,7 +201,7 @@ sleep 4
 screenshot -s -f png /boot/home/ui-efi.png
 hey Installer ALTB of Window 0 with which="int32(0)" > /dev/null
 ok "Install EFI loader invoked (the host checks the ESP)"
-md5sum /boot/system/data/platform_loaders/haiku_loader.efi | cut -d' ' -f1 \
+md5sum /boot/system/haiku_loader.efi | cut -d' ' -f1 \
 	> /tmp/loader.md5
 
 # the installed system runs the boot checks and lets us in at its first boot
